  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d Milj&#xf6;ministeriet Albanien</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Ministry of Environment Albania - New Environmnet Albania - New strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Albania needs to increase its preparations for the coming EU-negotiations and the Ministry of Tourism and Environment (MTE) is coordinating the work. Swedish support to the MTE and other institutions is instrumental in this process by its systematic  analysis of needs and identification of prioritized actions. The proposed environmental program covers a number of key planning documents required in the negotiation process and needed capacity building. 

The program will run over a two year period and has a budget of 20.3 million SEK.

The contribution shall achieve the following four main results:

1. Harmonization of the strategic framework in the Environmental sector/for Chapter 27; development of a cross-sector strategy for Environment and climate as well as development of 6 Directive Specific Implementation Plans (DSIPs).
2. Strengthened legal transpostion process; development of transponsition methodoloyg y and plan.
3. Strengthened institutional system and administrative capacities in the sector; institutional analysis and development of an institutional development plan, including capacity building.
4. Financing needs for Chapter 27; development of a financial strategy/plan for Chapter 27.

The agreement partner is the Ministry of Finance and Economy (MFE) which is the case for all agreements within the development cooperation in Albania. The MFE and its Central Financing and Contracting Unit (CFCU) will together with the Ministry of Tourism and Environment implement the Project (CFCU being responsible for procurement and contract management). Sida will disburse funds to MFE/CFCU which will make payments to the procured implementing Consultant. The budget will be revised after the project&apos;s inception phase and approved by Sida.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Albanien har ett stort behov av f&#xf6;rberedelser f&#xf6;r kommande EU-f&#xf6;rhandlingar och milj&#xf6;ministeriet ansvarar f&#xf6;r koordineringen av arbetet. Det svenska st&#xf6;det  till milj&#xf6;ministeriet och andra albanska institutioner har en nyckelroll i denna process genom det svenska st&#xf6;dets systematiska sektoransats och analys av de f&#xf6;rhandlingsrelaterade behoven samt identifiering av prioriterat givarst&#xf6;d. 

F&#xf6;reslaget milj&#xf6;program omfattar ett antal nyckeldokument f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rhandlingarna och behov av kompetensutveckling. Programmet kommer att l&#xf6;pa &#xf6;ver en tv&#xe5;-&#xe5;rsperiod och har en budget p&#xe5; 20.3 MSEK.

St&#xf6;det ska resultera i f&#xf6;ljande huvudresultat:
1. Harmonisering av det strategiska ramverket; framtagande av &#xf6;vergripande milj&#xf6;- och klimatstrategi samt 6 Directive Specific Implementation Plans (DSIPs).
2. F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt legal harmonisering/transponeringsprocess; framtagande av transponeringsmetodik samt transponeringsplan.
3. F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt institutionellt system och organisatorisk kapacitet; institutionell analys samt framtagande av institutionell utvecklings plan inklusive kapacitetsutveckling.
4. Finansiering av genomf&#xf6;rande av kapitel 27; framtagande av finansieringsstrategi/-plan f&#xf6;r kapitel 27.

Sidas avtalspartner &#xe4;r finansministeriet, vilket &#xe4;r fallet f&#xf6;r alla bist&#xe5;ndsprojekt i Albanien. Finansministeriet och dess CFCU (Central Financing and Contracting Unit) tillsammans
med milj&#xf6;ministeriet ansvarar f&#xf6;r projektgenomf&#xf6;randet (ansvaret regleras i en projektmanual) d&#xe4;r CFCU ansvarar f&#xf6;r upphandling och kontraktshantering. Sida betalar ut projektmedel till Finansministeriet som i sin tur betalar upphandlad projektgenomf&#xf6;rare/-konsult efter godk&#xe4;nd rapportering. Projektets budget kommer att revideras efter projektets inceptionsfas och godk&#xe4;nnas av Sida.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the contribution is to advance Albania&apos;s preparations for EU-negotiations by developing a set of strategic planning documents (policy, strategies and plans) and to increase administrative capacities to work with the long-term planning for reaching EU-standards.
The program has four short-term outcomes:
1.&#xa0;National political and strategic framework in the environment and climate change sector, drafted, consulted with stakeholders and approved by the responsible institutions.
2.&#xa0;Transposition process of EU directives in the environmental sector within the domestic legislation organized and properly planned.
3.&#xa0;Functional and institutional organization properly designed, ensuring clear responsibilities with no overlapping and provision of missing functions, including procedures guaranteeing coordination among institutions and internal structures, the proper planning of human resources/capacity development and of infrastructural/technological needs.
4. An integrated Financing Plan for the environment sector, prepared and communicated,&#xa0;serving as a baseline to ensure the proper funding for achieving EU environmental standards.</narrative>
  </description>
